  <!-- ── Method ───────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section id="method" class="tool-section">
    <div class="section-label">Method</div>
    <h2 class="section-title">Framework &amp; method</h2>

    <div class="tool-entries">
      <div class="tool-entry">
        <div class="tool-entry__overline">The harmony formulas</div>
        <p class="tool-entry__body">Working in HSL, hold saturation and lightness and rotate hue H by fixed angles. Complementary: H, H+180°. Analogous: H±30°. Triadic: H+120°, +240°. Split-complementary: H+150°, +210°. Tetradic: H+60°, +180°, +240°. Monochromatic: H fixed, lightness stepped ±15° and ±30°.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="tool-entry">
        <div class="tool-entry__overline">Nearest-Pantone snapping</div>
        <p class="tool-entry__body">A rotated hue is an abstract point, not a real swatch. To keep every palette Pantone-real, each computed colour is converted sRGB → XYZ → CIELAB and matched to the minimum-ΔE colour across the full library. ΔE is the reported perceptual distance; lower means a closer match.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="tool-entry">
        <div class="tool-entry__overline">Curation, not generation</div>
        <p class="tool-entry__body">Categories mirror how Pantone itself groups colour: one annual hue, ten runway standouts per season, seasonless neutrals, and hue families. Groupings within the Colour of the Year archive are editorial, sorted by chromatic mood.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="tool-entry">
        <div class="tool-entry__overline">On the data</div>
        <p class="tool-entry__body">Colour of the Year and Fashion Colour Trend Report hues are the published Pantone selections; swatch hex values come from the 2,310-colour Fashion, Home + Interiors reference set. Trend readings are computed from those values — screens can only approximate a dyed Pantone standard.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="note-line" id="srcs"></p>
    <p class="note-line">Colour selections © Pantone LLC, cited for reference. Built as an interactive reading experience.</p>
  </section>

